# Scout environment variables
# Copy to .env.local and fill in the two values below. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Local Scout needs ONLY the Supabase project URL + anon key. There is no
# Anthropic key and no web-search key: the loopback companion (packages/agent)
# shells out to your local `claude` CLI, which authenticates from its own
# keychain (see the README "Environment variables" section).

# --- Required (public — ships in the static client bundle; RLS protects rows) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Supabase Edge Function secrets — NOT set in this file ---
# The functions in `supabase/functions/*` read a few admin/deploy-only secrets.
# These live in the Supabase platform and are configured with
# `supabase secrets set …` (see `supabase/README.md`) — the Next.js app never
# reads them, so leave them out of `.env.local`. In particular a service-role
# key must never sit next to the client bundle. Listed here as a deploy
# reference only:
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   # admin client used by the companion-token and
#                               #   exa-search functions
#   EXA_API_KEY                 # optional — shared-key mode for the exa-search
#                               #   proxy; if unset the proxy returns
#                               #   403 byo_key_required (users supply their own)
#   EXA_DAILY_CAP               # optional — per-user daily cap for exa-search
#                               #   (defaults to 50)
